import OzakiTC.ADPLabels

/-! # The Z3 ADP model's test-level checks on its own inputs

The inputs of the Z3 model's test-level checks (`ozaki-NVIDIA/tests.py`) that concern particular
matrices, run through the unmodified Z3 model by `scripts/z3_adp_labels.py` and recorded as
binary64 words in [`data/z3-adp-labels.json`](../../data/z3-adp-labels.json). Each check below is
a kernel evaluation of the Lean routine on the same inputs.

| Label | Case | Z3 model | Lean |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `[T.1]` | decode edge values, `±0` | `x = m · 2^(e − 52)` | the same `(m, e)`; `decode_zeros` |
| `[T.3]` | slice counts for `53` bits | naive `8`, remap `7`, floor `7` | the same |
| `[T.4]` | `signed` case, three encodings | identical `C`, `8`, `8`, `9` slices | the same `C` and counts |
| `[T.7]` | exponent spans `3` and `10` | emulated, ESC `5` and `17` | the same path, ESC, `W`, slices, `C` |
| `[T.8]` | Test 2, `n = 8`, `b = 0` and `64` | fixed `W = 55` passes Grade A at `0`, fails at `64` | the same `C`, pass and failure |
| `[T.10]` | every entry `1e200` | emulated, `C = +Inf` | emulated, no values; native also none |
| `[T.11]` | subnormal entries | emulated | the same `C`, Grade A; `adpSafe` native |
| `[T.12]` | identity | native-slow, `C = I` | the same |

`[T.2]`, `[T.5]` and `[T.12]`'s zero policies are theorems (`Ozaki.ADP.paper_remap_example`,
`Ozaki.ADP.escCoarse_one`, `Ozaki.ADP.zeros_case_caught`, `Ozaki.ADP.field0_case_caught`). -/

